From 8fb1e1d5d5a7ff97558b24f60dff8214ff683e5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:00:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): review follow-ups for the all-walled chain card
 [daveey]

Independent review of #3855 at 06661a7 (APPROVE, non-blocking findings), all addressed:
- A chain is recorded as one (walls, failure_resets_at) by what quota_refusal_walls read (more than one
  route, or a rate-limited pin), not by the raw error's type, so a wrapped chain cannot split card and toast.
- A fallback that repeats the pin with an earlier reset relabels it as that quota wall, not "rate-limited".
- A chain sets the client's reset_at to its earliest reset when the pin's pool named a later one.
- A chain nested in a chain is rejected explicitly (a ProviderFallbackError is an AuthError and could pass
  as a rate-limited pin); a fallback whose reset has already passed disqualifies the chain.
- _requested_model reads resume_runtime_overrides.model_override (it has no `model` key).
- One clock for the recorded route and the toast; a chain entry named "auto" (agent_init) takes the
  refusal's own provider; repeated routes compare providers case-insensitively.

Tests, RED on 06661a7's source and GREEN after: typed-quota pin chain wording, a repeated pin relabelled,
past-reset and nested rate-limited chains stay generic, the chain's reset as client reset_at and the replay
clock (trusted_resets_at). Also added: a wait given only as "retry after Ns" text, a malformed walls record.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
